Frontend
- React 18 with Vite 5 as the dev server/bundler (plain JavaScript/JSX — no TypeScript)
- Radix UI primitives (alert dialog, dropdown menu, tooltip) with lucide-react icons
- react-dropzone for file uploads
- Document handling in the browser: pdfjs-dist (PDF parsing), mammoth (.docx → HTML), docx (generating Word files), jszip + file-saver for bundling/downloading

Backend (BFF)
- Express 5 running on Node 20+, acting as a backend-for-frontend that also proxies the Pomelo TechOps API (port 3001)
- PostgreSQL via pg, with its own migrate/seed scripts (db:migrate, db:seed) — currently not connected locally since DATABASE_URL is unset
- Auth: JWT (jsonwebtoken) + bcryptjs password hashing, cookies via cookie-parser
- Hardening: helmet, cors, express-rate-limit; input validation with zod
- Sentry for error tracking on both the React app and the Node server

Tooling & quality
- Playwright for E2E tests
- ESLint 9 + Prettier, enforced pre-commit through husky + lint-staged
- concurrently powers npm run dev:all to run the BFF and Vite together

In short: a React/Vite SPA with an Express BFF in one repo, Postgres underneath, JWT auth, and a document-processing focus (PDF/Word) — matching its purpose as an internal IT support portal (tickets, docs, admin tools).
